Analyze the following security patch diff for Kernel Memory Corruption (Use-After-Free) (CVE-2024-KERNEL-UAF).

Pre-Patch Vulnerable Code:
```
static void cleanup_session(struct sock_session *sess) {
    kfree(sess->rx_buffer);
    // Missing pointer nullification before unlock allows concurrent thread access
    mutex_unlock(&sess->lock);
}
```

Git Patch Diff:
```diff
@@ -14,3 +14,5 @@ static void cleanup_session(struct sock_session *sess) {
     mutex_lock(&sess->lock);
-    kfree(sess->rx_buffer);
+    struct rx_buf *tmp = sess->rx_buffer;
+    sess->rx_buffer = NULL;
+    kfree(tmp);
     mutex_unlock(&sess->lock);
```

